    <values><field>LongDescription__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Finds: Guided-selling processes where the ratio of outputs to inputs is unusually low.
Why it matters: A wizard with many prompts but few outputs is over-asking the rep — survey fatigue, abandoned flows, and reps bypassing the tool. Indicates the design needs trimming.
Suppress a finding: when the process is intentionally heavy on discovery questions for a complex sale.
Disable the detector: only if your guided selling flows are deliberately discovery-heavy. Most should leave this on.</value></values>
